/* Version script for q.so (the bionic Q linker plugin loaded by
 * libhybris-common.so). Without this, q.so exported ~527 default-
 * visibility symbols including `__tls_get_addr`, `strlcpy`, `strlcat`
 * -- names that collide with host glibc/ld.so. The actual public ABI
 * is just `android_*`: entry points the libhybris-common dlopen/dlsym
 * shim looks up via dlsym(linker_handle, ...) in
 * hooks.c::__hybris_load_linker. Vendor libraries loaded via
 * hybris_dlopen don't link against q.so directly -- their unresolved
 * symbols (including all libdl ABI like __loader_dlopen,
 * __loader_dlsym, __loader_shared_globals) are resolved through
 * libhybris-common's _get_hooked_symbol table, never via dlsym
 * against q.so, so the historical __loader_ and __linker_ exports
 * were unreachable dead weight.
 *
 * Everything else (linker internals, bionic libc helpers, the TLSDESC
 * resolver, exception-handling glue, std::string / std::vector
 * instantiations) becomes local. Hiding `__tls_get_addr` specifically
 * closes the
 *   "self-PLT call inside q.so accidentally binds to glibc's
 *    __tls_get_addr because libhybris-common links against glibc"
 * failure class at the link level instead of relying on us never
 * regressing the TLSDESC-always-promote-to-static fix in linker.cpp.
 */
{
  global:
    android_*;
  local:
    *;
};
